Disclosed are a compact electrochemical cell and a process for fabricating it. The process comprises:

- producing one or more internal electrodes from an electron-conductive or semiconductive material, M1;
- supplying a hollow substrate formed from an electrically insulating material, M6, with at least one internal passage;
- coating the substrate’s outer surface with an electrically conductive material, M2;
- arranging colloidal particles of an electrically insulating material, M3, as a template over the M2 coating;
- applying an electrically conductive layer of material M4 onto the M2 layer;
- forming a layer L1 of an electron-conductive or semiconductive material, M5, over the M4 layer;
- inserting the at least one internal electrode into the corresponding internal passage of the resulting assembly;
- securing both open ends of the assembly using an electrically insulating material, M7; and
- eliminating the M2, M3, M4, and M6 materials.
